            "heading": "<strong>Tongue Stabilization</strong>",
            "heading_size": "h1"
          }
        },
        "text_Ah3HWY": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Tongue stabilization is the quiet mechanism that makes RelorGuard stop snoring so effectively. When you fall asleep, the tongue naturally relaxes and tends to fall backward, narrowing the airway and creating vibration. RelorGuard gently moves the lower jaw forward, and because the tongue is attached to the jaw, it follows that movement — shifting slightly forward and staying stable instead of collapsing. With the tongue held in this supported position, the airway stays open, airflow becomes smooth, and the vibration that causes snoring disappears.</p>",
            "text_style": "body"
          }
        }
      },
